  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1056 PM CDT MON OCT 12 2026\n\nBroad high pressure is going to persist through much of this week\nleading to above normal high temperatures each day. With the dry\nair mass in place, overnight lows are expected to drop into the\nupper 50s to low 60s each morning, but those cool mornings will\nwarm up quickly after sunrise with several locations approaching\nor breaking high temperature records for this time of year.\n\nA trough moves through the Midwest Friday into Saturday and will\npush a dry cold front southeastward through Central AL Friday\nnight into Saturday morning. Little to no rain is expected from\nthis, but much cooler temperatures will advect into the region\nSaturday through Sunday.\n\n25/Owen",
